# Anti-Slop UI

Do not produce generic AI-generated interfaces.

Avoid defaulting to:

- purple/blue gradients
- excessive rounded cards
- excessive glassmorphism
- huge hero sections
- excessive shadows
- floating blobs
- decorative gradient text
- three-column card grids everywhere
- every section inside a card
- excessive badges
- meaningless icons
- oversized headings
- excessive pill-shaped controls
- generic dashboard layouts
- arbitrary animated backgrounds
- unnecessary illustrations
- "AI-looking" visual language

Do not add decoration merely because the page feels empty.

Instead improve:

- typography
- spacing
- composition
- hierarchy
- content
- alignment
- contrast
- information architecture

## Cards

Cards are not the default container for every piece of content.

Use cards when they create a meaningful grouping or interaction boundary.

Do not cardify everything.

## Color

Do not introduce a large palette.

Prefer a restrained system with deliberate accents.

## Radius

Do not use large border radii everywhere.

Use radius according to component semantics.

## Shadows

Use shadows sparingly.

Elevation should communicate hierarchy, not decoration.

## Motion

Do not animate everything.

Motion must communicate:

- state
- causality
- hierarchy
- continuity
- feedback

## Rule

If a visual element could be removed without reducing comprehension, interaction, or brand expression, question whether it belongs.